* ==============================================================================
* IBM MQ 9.4 - Auckland Gateway Configuration for Outbound Sydney Route (QM_AKL_FR)
* Run this on QM_AKL_FR to route cross-border payments to Sydney!
* ==============================================================================

* 1. Define Transmission Queue for Sydney
* This queue holds messages temporarily before they are transmitted to Sydney.
DEFINE QLOCAL(QM_SYD) USAGE(XMITQ) REPLACE

* 2. Define Remote Queue Definition
* When Spring Boot or ACE sends to PAYMENT.CROSSBORDER.OUT on Auckland Gateway,
* MQ will automatically route it to QM_SYD's PAYMENT.CROSSBORDER.OUT via the transmission queue.
DEFINE QREMOTE(PAYMENT.CROSSBORDER.OUT) +
  RNAME(PAYMENT.CROSSBORDER.OUT) +
  RQMNAME(QM_SYD) +
  XMITQ(QM_SYD) +
  REPLACE

* 3. Define Sender Channel to Sydney
* REPLACE <VMWARE_UBUNTU_NODE_IP> with the IP address of one of your Ubuntu VM nodes.
* Note: Port 31414 is the NodePort exposed by our Kubernetes service.
DEFINE CHANNEL(AKL.TO.SYD) CHLTYPE(SDR) TRPTYPE(TCP) +
  CONNAME('YOUR_VMWARE_UBUNTU_NODE_IP(31414)') +
  XMITQ(QM_SYD) +
  DESCR('Sender Channel to Sydney K8s MQ Instance') +
  REPLACE

* 4. Start the Sender Channel
* Once Sydney MQ is running on K8s and the Node IP is configured, start the channel!
* START CHANNEL(AKL.TO.SYD)
